      "body": "Hey everyone,\n\nWorking with sensitive documents and code daily, I got incredibly frustrated with \"free\" online converters. Whether it's a PDF-to-Image tool, a JSON formatter, or a password generator, almost all of them secretly upload your files to a remote server.\n\nTo solve this, I spent the last few weeks building [Mini-Tools.uk](https://mini-tools.uk/).\n\nIt’s a minimalist suite of 20+ everyday web utilities designed with a strict privacy-first approach. By using modern browser APIs, everything processes 100% locally on your machine. ✨ Core Features:\n\nZero Server Uploads: Your files and data never leave your browser. You can literally load the page, disconnect from the Wi-Fi, and it still works perfectly.\n\nDeveloper & Everyday Tools: Includes PDF extractors, JSON auto-fix formatters, secure password generators, and AI Prompt helpers.\n\nNo-BS Experience: No ads, no sign-ups, and completely free.\n\nI built this to scratch my own itch, but I’m sharing it in hopes it helps others who care about digital privacy. Would love to hear your feedback or requests for new tools!\n\nCheck it out: https://mini-tools.uk/",
